    "created_at": "2022-02-14T15:28:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-02-14T15:28:11Z",
    "body": "Note that that part only deals with *closing the connection*. How about opening which is the situation where the error could happen before the `ws.on(\"error\", ...)` can be executed?\r\n\r\nI think there should be something similar in the steps for the constructor of WebSocket(). It currently just says that the connection can be opened in parallel without talking anything about queueing a task which I would have expected. If it said that the task to open a new socket must be queued as a task there would be no issue.",
