    "created_at": "2022-02-14T15:31:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-02-14T15:31:28Z",
    "body": "As I read the current spec, it would allow opening a new socket without syncronization and if local software firewall kills the connection, it could happen (in theory) before the `ws.on(\"error\", ...)` is executed. I understand that the `close` event cannot fire until the browser native event queue has run so listening for `close` event should always work with current spec.",
