    "created_at": "2022-02-14T19:00:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-02-14T19:00:22Z",
    "body": "The relevant section is under [feedback from the protocol](https://websockets.spec.whatwg.org/#feedback-from-the-protocol):\r\n\r\n> When [the WebSocket connection is closed](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6455#section-7.1.4), possibly [cleanly](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6455#page-41:~:text=closed-,_cleanly_.), the user agent must [queue a task](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#queue-a-task) to run the following substeps:\r\n> \r\n> 1. Change the [readyState](https://websockets.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-websocket-readystate) attribute’s value to [CLOSED](https://websockets.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-websocket-closed) (3).\r\n> \r\n> 2. If the user agent was required to [fail the WebSocket connection](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6455#section-7.1.7), or if [the WebSocket connection was closed](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6455#section-7.1.4) after being flagged as full, [fire an event](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire) named [error](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/indices.html#event-error) at the [WebSocket](https://websockets.spec.whatwg.org/#websocket) object. [[WSP]](https://websockets.spec.whatwg.org/#biblio-wsp)\r\n\r\nIt clearly says that a task is queued to fire the error event.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
